  "id": "COMPOUND:27962 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "n-Octyl sulfate is implicated in a complex network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the target of SQ20B. The evidence suggests that n-Octyl sulfate acts as a target for multiple enzymes, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is also a target of 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These enzymes are part of a pathway that culminates in the activation of SQ20B. The presence of multiple intermediates in this chain indicates a potential mechanism where n-Octyl sulfate may influence the activity of these enzymes, thereby affecting SQ20B. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on specific molecular targets, suggesting that n-Octyl sulfate could exert its effects through a series of enzymatic interactions that ultimately lead to SQ20B activation.",
